---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Icon from "../../components/Icon.astro";

const title = "Jio WiFi not working? Fixes for JioFiber and AirFiber";
const description = "Jio WiFi shows connected but nothing loads? Step by step fixes for JioFiber, AirFiber and JioFi, plus a one click Chrome option.";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://arverma.dev/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Guides", item: "https://arverma.dev/guides/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Jio WiFi not working", item: "https://arverma.dev/guides/jio-wifi-not-working/" },
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="section guide-page">
    <p class="section-label"><Icon name="book-open" size={14} />Guide</p>
    <h1 class="guide-title">Jio WiFi not working? Fixes for JioFiber and AirFiber</h1>
    
    <div class="guide-content">
      <p class="guide-lead">
        Your Jio WiFi says connected, but pages will not load. This happens on JioFiber, JioAirFiber and JioFi when 
        the connection goes idle or the router loses sync with the network. Here is what to check, in order.
      </p>

      <h2 class="guide-h2"><Icon name="info" size={16} />JioFiber vs AirFiber vs JioFi</h2>
      <p>
        JioFiber is the wired fiber broadband service. The fiber cable plugs into your router, and you get speeds 
        from 30 Mbps to 1 Gbps depending on your plan.
      </p>
      <p>
        JioAirFiber is the wireless 5G fixed broadband service. No fiber cable. The router connects to Jio's 5G 
        network over the air. It works in areas where fiber is not available.
      </p>
      <p>
        JioFi is a portable WiFi hotspot device. It uses a SIM card and connects to the mobile network. 
        If you have a JioFi, most of this guide still applies, but check the JioFi battery and SIM first.
      </p>

      <h2 class="guide-h2"><Icon name="activity" size={16} />Lights and what they mean</h2>
      <p>
        On a JioFiber router, look for these lights:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Power:</strong> Should be solid green. If off, check the power cable.</li>
        <li><strong>PON or Fiber:</strong> Should be solid green. If off or red, the fiber cable is disconnected 
        or there is a network issue. Check the fiber cable at the back of the router and where it enters your home.</li>
        <li><strong>LAN or WiFi:</strong> Should be solid or blinking green when devices are connected.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        On JioAirFiber, the lights work differently because there is no fiber cable. Check the 5G signal light. 
        If it is red or blinking, the router is not getting a good 5G signal. Move the router closer to a window 
        or higher up.
      </p>

      <h2 class="guide-h2"><Icon name="settings" size={16} />192.168.29.1 router page</h2>
      <p>
        Open a browser and go to <a href="http://192.168.29.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">192.168.29.1<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span></a>. 
        This is the router admin page. The default username is usually <code>admin</code> and the password is on 
        the sticker on the back of the router.
      </p>
      <p>
        Check the WAN or Internet status. If it says disconnected, the router is not getting an IP from Jio. 
        Restart the router and wait 2 minutes. If it still says disconnected, call Jio support.
      </p>

      <h2 class="guide-h2"><Icon name="smartphone" size={16} />Plan and recharge check in MyJio</h2>
      <p>
        Open the MyJio app. Go to your JioFiber or AirFiber connection and check the plan status. If your plan has 
        expired or your account is suspended, the internet will not work even if WiFi is connected.
      </p>
      <p>
        Recharge if needed. It can take 5 to 10 minutes for the connection to come back after a recharge.
      </p>

      <h2 class="guide-h2"><Icon name="refresh-cw" size={16} />Restart order</h2>
      <p>
        Turn off the router. Wait 30 seconds. Turn it back on and wait 2 minutes for all lights to stabilize. 
        This clears the connection state and forces the router to get a fresh link from Jio.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you have a separate ONT (the small box where the fiber cable comes in), restart that first, wait 30 seconds, 
        then restart the router.
      </p>

      <h2 class="guide-h2"><Icon name="zap" size={16} />Stuck connection and WiFi Hammer</h2>
      <p>
        Sometimes the router goes idle and does not wake up when you try to load a page. This happens more on JioFiber 
        than on other ISPs in my experience.
      </p>
      <p>
        I built <a href="/projects/wifi-hammer/">WiFi Hammer</a> to fix this. It is a Chrome extension that wakes 
        the connection with one click. You can also turn on Auto-hammer to keep the connection fresh every 30 minutes. 
        It works by sending a small network request that forces the router to reset the link.
      </p>
      <p>
        WiFi Hammer does not make your internet faster or increase your plan speed. It only wakes a stuck connection.
      </p>

      <h2 class="guide-h2"><Icon name="phone" size={16} />Jio support</h2>
      <p>
        If none of the above work, contact Jio support:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Call <strong>198</strong> from your Jio mobile number, or <strong>1800-889-9999</strong> from any phone.</li>
        <li>Use the MyJio app: Go to Help > Chat with us.</li>
        <li>Visit the <a href="https://www.jio.com/help/jiofiber" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Jio Help Center<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span></a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        When you call, tell them your router lights are on but you cannot load any pages. They can reset your connection 
        from their side or schedule a technician visit.
      </p>

      <h2 class="guide-h2"><Icon name="help-circle" size={16} />FAQ</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-q">Why does my JioFiber say connected but nothing loads?</h3>
          <p class="faq-a">
            This usually happens when the router goes idle and does not wake up, or when the fiber link is down. 
            Check the PON light on the router. If it is red or off, the fiber cable is disconnected.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-q">What is the difference between JioFiber and JioAirFiber?</h3>
          <p class="faq-a">
            JioFiber uses a physical fiber cable. JioAirFiber connects to Jio's 5G network wirelessly. JioAirFiber 
            works in areas where fiber is not available yet.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-q">How do I check my JioFiber plan status?</h3>
          <p class="faq-a">
            Open the MyJio app, go to your JioFiber connection, and check the plan details. If your plan has expired, 
            recharge it in the app or on the Jio website.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-q">What does the PON light mean?</h3>
          <p class="faq-a">
            PON stands for Passive Optical Network. If the PON light is green, the fiber link is working. 
            If it is red or off, the fiber cable is disconnected or there is a network issue.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-q">Will WiFi Hammer work with JioFiber?</h3>
          <p class="faq-a">
            Yes. WiFi Hammer works with any broadband or router, including JioFiber and JioAirFiber. It wakes a stuck 
            connection when pages will not load even though WiFi says connected.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="guide-related">
        <h3 class="guide-related-title">Related guides</h3>
        <ul class="guide-related-list">
          <li><a href="/guides/wifi-connected-no-internet/"><Icon name="arrow-right" size={14} />WiFi connected but no internet: 8 fixes that work</a></li>
          <li><a href="/guides/airtel-wifi-not-working/"><Icon name="arrow-right" size={14} />Airtel WiFi not working? Fixes for Xstream Fiber</a></li>
          <li><a href="/projects/wifi-hammer/"><Icon name="arrow-right" size={14} />WiFi Hammer Chrome extension</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .guide-page {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .guide-title {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1.5rem 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .guide-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .guide-lead {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .guide-content p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .guide-content ul {
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .guide-content li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .guide-content code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: 0.125rem 0.375rem;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
  }

  .guide-content a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .guide-content a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-2);
  }

  .guide-h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .faq-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .faq-item {
    padding: 1rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
  }

  .faq-q {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .faq-a {
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .guide-related {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
  }

  .guide-related-title {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .guide-related-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .guide-related-list a {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .guide-related-list a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .guide-title {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
